    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d115">

                <pb facs="0330" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.F.M. Files: Lot
                    M–88: Box 2061: CFM Documents</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the United States
                            Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                            Ministers</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.F.M. (46) 62</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-05-08">8 May, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Future Procedure of
                    Council</hi></p>
                <p>The Council of Foreign Ministers, having discussed many unsettled issues involved
                    in the proposed treaties and having settled some of these and having been unable
                    at the present time to resolve others of them, have decided: <list>
                        <label><hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                        <item>To direct the Deputies to prepare drafts of the treaties on the basis
                            of existing decisions and of such further agreements which may be
                            reached by the Deputies and to report on matters on which there is no
                            agreement; and</item>
                        <label><hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                        <item>To call, in accordance with the agreement reached at Moscow, a Peace
                            conference to meet in Paris on 15th June, to which draft treaties shall
                            be submitted so that in the final drafting of the treaties the Council
                            shall have the benefit and assistance of recommendations made by the
                            Peace Conference.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>, 10 May, 1946.<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d115-f1"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d115-f1" n="86" xml:id="d115-f1-content">
                <p>This proposal was originally circulated to the Council of Foreign Ministers
                    during its 13th Meeting, May 8, 1946, 11 a.m.; see the United States Delegation
                    Record of that meeting, <ref target="#pg298">p. 298</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
